      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my 2018 civic makes this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas to accelerate. i think it might be a belt issue but i'm not sure. can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why it would make that kind of sound if it's going bad?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt in your 2018 Civic is responsible for driving various accessories attached to your engine, such as the alternator, power steering pump, and air conditioning compressor. If this belt is worn or damaged, it can make a squealing noise during acceleration, because it's slipping or getting caught on something. A broken or worn belt can also cause engine damage due to loss of power to these accessories. It's wise to inspect the belt for signs of wear, adjustments to tension, or look into replacing it if needed.",
